`never` is a type in TypeScript that represents a value that will never occur. It is used to indicate that a function or branch of code will never return a value, or that a variable will never have a value assigned to it. For example, a function that throws an error and never returns a value can be given the type `never`. Using `never` can help catch errors and improve the type safety of your code.

